{"id": "EUVD-2026-32458", "enisaUuid": "a12e4900-d1e4-38ce-b6be-c393584eab73", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nKVM: nSVM: Raise #UD if unhandled VMMCALL isn't intercepted by L1\n\nExplicitly synthesize a #UD for VMMCALL if L2 is active, L1 does NOT want\nto intercept VMMCALL, nested_svm_l2_tlb_flush_enabled() is true, and the\nhypercall is something other than one of the supported Hyper-V hypercalls.\nWhen all of the above conditions are met, KVM will intercept VMMCALL but\nnever forward it to L1, i.e. will let L2 make hypercalls as if it were L1.\n\nThe TLFS says a whole lot of nothing about this scenario, so go with the\narchitectural behavior, which says that VMMCALL #UDs if it's not\nintercepted.\n\nOpportunistically do a 2-for-1 stub trade by stub-ifying the new API\ninstead of the helpers it uses.  The last remaining \"single\" stub will\nsoon be dropped as well.\n\n[sean: rewrite changelog and comment, tag for stable, remove defunct stubs]", "datePublished": "2026-05-27T12:58:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:41:18", "baseScore": 7.9, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fcef67506c0234935cb0fb026740a637edb58d7c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/924d721fae95687acedbaf624a094ed0e8b67104", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/009c0f726abeaa67aad1d96b883bdce01d405ce2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5fb4a5f361565f5b629d8a8fe5288ce8463c5727", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c36991c6f8d2ab56ee67aff04e3c357f45cfc76c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gj33-hwgc-v3v8", "CVE-2026-46076"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "231184a0-5b40-33be-9c97-7e24192cb739", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2a850207-f1a5-3e6b-97e3-1a6e8cfe5bb5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.27"}, {"id": "40fa0da2-15d7-302a-bc69-c2222a12242d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "4d68b79b-96b1-3656-9b9f-3cf5e46c2a9a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "6b24e992-dbb4-3b3e-a544-ac159f5cd471", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3f4a812edf5cb0a50e65fbdfafdb3e688da18f16 <924d721fae95687acedbaf624a094ed0e8b67104"}, {"id": "8464e0db-63e3-3d04-ab5e-f08cd8fb99e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.4"}, {"id": "860a7592-3704-3139-9865-a15bc0872713", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3f4a812edf5cb0a50e65fbdfafdb3e688da18f16 <fcef67506c0234935cb0fb026740a637edb58d7c"}, {"id": "b1325c0b-4bdc-3cac-8775-67e402205f16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3f4a812edf5cb0a50e65fbdfafdb3e688da18f16 <5fb4a5f361565f5b629d8a8fe5288ce8463c5727"}, {"id": "c697de8f-0142-3747-9099-658e1b956b59", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3f4a812edf5cb0a50e65fbdfafdb3e688da18f16 <009c0f726abeaa67aad1d96b883bdce01d405ce2"}, {"id": "e25c2010-812b-35a5-a83c-cd299bad6ce1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.2"}, {"id": "e5544d64-a025-3e14-b8f5-f3d70591fbc5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.86"}, {"id": "fa15983f-1359-31fb-ad7a-cd736e0b3a8b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "3f4a812edf5cb0a50e65fbdfafdb3e688da18f16 <c36991c6f8d2ab56ee67aff04e3c357f45cfc76c"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "7734c872-b6ba-35c8-a627-7a4b1f020af5", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}